@startuml
' Train and inference/evaluation circuits of the planned bmiemg.models package.
' Kept apart from activity.puml so the download/prune flow stays readable.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam activity {
    BackgroundColor #F8F8F8
    BorderColor #333333
    FontColor #111111
}
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FFF8DC
    BorderColor #999999
}

legend right
|= Colour |= Meaning |
|<#D6EAF8> | User command / function call |
|<#FADBD8> | User manual edit or file placement |
|<#D5F5E3> | System action |
|<#F5B7B1> | Error / failed validation |
|<#FFF8DC> | Artefact note |
endlegend

|#E8F1FF|User|
|#EAF7EA|System|

'=============================================================================='
'TRAIN circuit'
'=============================================================================='
|#E8F1FF|User|
start
:Run prune export (data/dataset/<protocol>/client, server); <<#D6EAF8>>
:Write configs/model/train/<name>.yaml; <<#FADBD8>>
:Run ModelTrainer().run(name)\n(locally or as a cluster batch job); <<#D6EAF8>>

|#EAF7EA|System|
:Load TrainProtocol, resolve registry keys; <<#D5F5E3>>
if (Unknown key or invalid parameter?) then (yes)
    :Raise ValueError with allowed keys; <<#F5B7B1>>
    stop
else (no)
endif
:Seed python, numpy and torch; <<#D5F5E3>>
:DatasetReader reads client/train and client/val .fif\ninto PartitionData; <<#D5F5E3>>
:Apply input steps in order\n(notch, window 150 ms / 25 ms, target, features...)\n-> WindowSet; <<#D5F5E3>>
:Model.fit(train, val); <<#D5F5E3>>
:Score val WindowSet with val_metrics; <<#D5F5E3>>
:ArtifactStore saves weights, artifact.yaml\n(model key + params, inputs, classes, channels,\nsfreq, window, seed, dataset ref, git commit)\nand the resolved config; <<#D5F5E3>>
note right
  artifacts/models/<name>_<timestamp>/
  This folder is the hand-off to evaluation
  and to any later reduction stage.
end note
:Report writers write training report\n(curves, val metrics, model size); <<#D5F5E3>>

|#E8F1FF|User|
:Upload artifact folder to MAKE Archive\nand record its path; <<#FADBD8>>

'=============================================================================='
'INFERENCE / EVALUATION circuit'
'=============================================================================='
:Write configs/model/eval/<name>.yaml\n(artifact path, targets, metrics, schemes); <<#FADBD8>>
:Run ModelEvaluator().run(name); <<#D6EAF8>>

|#EAF7EA|System|
:ArtifactStore loads artifact.yaml and rebuilds\nthe Model and input steps from it; <<#D5F5E3>>
if (Dataset channels / sfreq match the artifact?) then (no)
    :Raise ValueError (artifact contract mismatch); <<#F5B7B1>>
    stop
else (yes)
endif
:DatasetReader reads the target partitions; <<#D5F5E3>>
:Apply the artifact's input steps -> WindowSet; <<#D5F5E3>>
:Model.predict -> Predictions; <<#D5F5E3>>
if (Target has labels?) then (client/test, markers zeroed)
    :Write blind predictions only; <<#D5F5E3>>
    :Join with server/test labels\n(server-side scoring); <<#D5F5E3>>
else (client/val or server/test)
endif
:Split Predictions by each EvaluationScheme\n(pooled, per_subject, per_class); <<#D5F5E3>>
:Compute every Metric per group\n(accuracy, cohen_kappa, f1, confusion_matrix); <<#D5F5E3>>
:Report writers write EvaluationReport\n(metrics json, predictions csv, plots); <<#D5F5E3>>
note right
  reports/<eval_name>_<timestamp>/
end note

|#E8F1FF|User|
:Compare reports across configs\n(baseline vs preprocessing study); <<#FADBD8>>
end
@enduml
